Backport Qt Multimedia's Wasm media-device re-entrancy and reconciliation
fixes to 6.11.1.

Upstream references (selected changes, not full-commit cherry-picks):
- 7f71286a9f22ae69936a21b561570c4ea1af2431
- 35b0ea686685cb591d598d503bfa110daf6c69e2
- 6cedb5d96f36c5d406d1bb58352dc05523c62fa4
- 9018988e854ce6b7689e716b4afe93d6173a135c
- 191cda01b86bc6b28e663426bb7a3eef6b2d39cc

The device reconciliation shape is adapted from 7f71286, but Qt 6.11 still
routes audio through OpenAL and must retain its device names as the default
source and sink. Reconcile browser devices on every enumeration while
excluding the two OpenAL fallback keys from stale removal. Extend the upstream
queued-notification fix to the two OpenAL callbacks and correct the
capture/playback cache-key typos.

Always enumerate through Promise callbacks, including JSPI builds. A
devicechange notification can be drained by a synchronous native input export,
where awaiting the JavaScript Promise would attempt to suspend through a
non-promising boundary. Serialize and coalesce enumeration requests so each
request owns a fresh callback bundle, repeated events never reuse a moved-from
callback, and an older result cannot arrive after and overwrite newer state.

